#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:69
msgid "`collections <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#collections>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:71
msgid ""
"The *OrderedDict* class is now implemented in C, which makes it 4 to 100 "
"times faster."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:73
msgid ""
"*OrderedDict.items()* , *OrderedDict.keys()* , *OrderedDict.values()* "
"views now support reversed() iteration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:76
msgid ""
"The deque class now defines *index()*, *insert()*, and *copy()*, and "
"supports the + and * operators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:78
msgid "Docstrings produced by namedtuple() can now be updated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:80
msgid ""
"The UserString class now implements the *__getnewargs__()*, *__rmod__()*,"
" *casefold()*, *format_map()*, *isprintable()*, and *maketrans()* methods"
" to match the corresponding methods of str."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:83
msgid "`heapq <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#heapq>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:85
msgid ""
"Element comparison in *merge()* can now be customized by passing a key "
"function in a new optional key keyword argument, and a new optional "
"*reverse* keyword argument can be used to reverse element comparison"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:88
msgid "`io <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#io>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:90
msgid ""
"A new *BufferedIOBase.readinto1()* method, that uses at most one call to "
"the underlying raw stream's *RawIOBase.read()* or *RawIOBase.readinto()* "
"methods"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:93
msgid "`json <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#json>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:95
msgid ""
"JSON decoder now raises JSONDecodeError instead of ValueError to provide "
"better context information about the error."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:98
msgid "`math <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#math>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:100
msgid "Two new constants have been added to the math module: *inf* and *nan*."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:102
msgid ""
"A new function *isclose()* provides a way to test for approximate "
"equality."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:104
msgid ""
"A new *gcd()* function has been added. The *fractions.gcd()* function is "
"now deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:106
msgid "`os <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#os>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:108
msgid ""
"The new *scandir()* function returning an iterator of DirEntry objects "
"has been added."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:110
msgid ""
"The *urandom()* function now uses the *getrandom()* syscall on Linux 3.17"
" or newer, and *getentropy()* on OpenBSD 5.6 and newer, removing the need"
" to use /dev/urandom and avoiding failures due to potential file "
"descriptor exhaustion."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:114
msgid ""
"New *get_blocking()* and *set_blocking()* functions allow getting and "
"setting a file descriptor's blocking mode (O_NONBLOCK.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:117
msgid ""
"There is a new *os.path.commonpath()* function returning the longest "
"common sub-path of each passed pathname"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:120
msgid "`re <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#re>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:122
msgid ""
"References and conditional references to groups with fixed length are now"
" allowed in lookbehind assertions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:124
msgid ""
"The number of capturing groups in regular expressions is no longer "
"limited to 100."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:126
msgid ""
"The *sub()* and *subn()* functions now replace unmatched groups with "
"empty strings instead of raising an exception."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:129
msgid ""
"The *re.error* exceptions have new attributes, msg, pattern, pos, lineno,"
" and colno, that provide better context information about the error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:132
msgid "`socket <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#socket>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:134
msgid ""
"Functions with timeouts now use a monotonic clock, instead of a system "
"clock."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:136
msgid ""
"A new *socket.sendfile()* method allows sending a file over a socket by "
"using the high-performance *os.sendfile()* function on UNIX, resulting in"
" uploads being from 2 to 3 times faster than when using plain "
"*socket.send()*"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:140
msgid ""
"The *socket.sendall()* method no longer resets the socket timeout every "
"time bytes are received or sent. The socket timeout is now the maximum "
"total duration to send all data."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:143
msgid ""
"The backlog argument of the *socket.listen()* method is now optional. By "
"default it is set to SOMAXCONN or to 128, whichever is less."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:146
msgid "`ssl <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#ssl>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:148
msgid "Memory BIO Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:150
msgid "Application-Layer Protocol Negotiation Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:152
msgid ""
"There is a new *SSLSocket.version()* method to query the actual protocol "
"version in use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:154
msgid "The SSLSocket class now implements a *SSLSocket.sendfile()* method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:156
msgid ""
"The *SSLSocket.send()* method now raises either the "
"*ssl.SSLWantReadError* or *ssl.SSLWantWriteError* exception on a non-"
"blocking socket if the operation would block. Previously, it would return"
" 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:159
msgid ""
"The *cert_time_to_seconds()* function now interprets the input time as "
"UTC and not as local time, per RFC 5280. Additionally, the return value "
"is always an int."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:162
msgid ""
"New *SSLObject.shared_ciphers()* and *SSLSocket.shared_ciphers()* methods"
" return the list of ciphers sent by the client during the handshake."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:165
msgid ""
"The *SSLSocket.do_handshake()*, *SSLSocket.read()*, "
"*SSLSocket.shutdown()*, and *SSLSocket.write()* methods of the SSLSocket "
"class no longer reset the socket timeout every time bytes are received or"
" sent."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:168
msgid "The *match_hostname()* function now supports matching of IP addresses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:170
msgid "`sys <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#sys>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:172
msgid ""
"A new *set_coroutine_wrapper()* function allows setting a global hook "
"that will be called whenever a coroutine object is created by an async "
"def function. A corresponding *get_coroutine_wrapper()* can be used to "
"obtain a currently set wrapper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:176
msgid ""
"A new *is_finalizing()* function can be used to check if the Python "
"interpreter is shutting down."
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:178
msgid "`time <https://docs.python.org/3/whatsnew/3.5.html#time>`_"
msgstr ""

#: ../../differences/python_35.rst:180
msgid "The *monotonic()* function is now always available"
msgstr ""

